{title: Long Way Through Winter}
{artist: The Cedar Line}
{key: E}

{start_of_intro: Intro}
[E]  [B]  [C#m]  [A]  (x2)
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Snow came early on th[B]e northern track
[C#m]Every station that w[A]e passed was black
[E]You had a ticket and [B]a borrowed coat
[C#m]And a song you only ha[A]lf remembered wrote
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]Somewhere after mid[B]night in the dining car
[C#m]We split a sandwich and [A]a broken guitar
[E]You played three chor[B]ds and the conductor sang
[C#m]Every window shook a[A]nd every bottle rang
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_prechorus: Pre-Chorus}
[F#m]Hold on, hold [A]on
[F#m]The morning's furt[B]her than it seems
{end_of_prechorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[E]It's a long [B]way through winter
[C#m]It's a long way [A]through the cold
[E]But I'd ride [B]it all again, love
[C#m]If it's yo[A]ur hand I h[E]old
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]Frozen rivers and [B]a sleeping town
[C#m]Engine coughing as t[A]he sun goes down
[E]Strangers trading ev[B]ery story they own
[C#m]Nobody on this train [A]is going home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_prechorus: Pre-Chorus}
[F#m]Hold on, hold [A]on
